      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Seasons are caused by the combination of axial tilt and revolution around the Sun.",
        "Distance from the Sun does NOT cause the change in seasons.",
        "Earth maintains a constant axial tilt of 23.5°.",
        "Parallelism ensures the Earth's axis always points in the same direction."
      ],
      "id": "xdgr1s5"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• 23.5° axial tilt.",
      "id": "uqa2ep7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Parallelism — axis always points in same direction.",
      "id": "twxdni4"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Exams frequently test the misconception that distance from the Sun causes seasons—remember it is caused by axial tilt and revolution.",
        "Note the exact value of Earth's axial tilt: 23.5°.",
        "Parallelism refers to the axis always pointing in the same direction throughout Earth's orbit."
      ],
      "id": "9mx168k"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Revolution around the Sun.",
      "id": "zg23ftv"
